- The framework (once, at run start) STAGES the references as files under `design/references/` and compiles an extracted SPEC (screens / endpoints / entities) into `design/reference_spec.json`. READ that spec first; then `view_image(...)` each staged screenshot before authoring UI from it (never author from memory when an image exists). If no references were provided, neither exists — proceed from the requirements.
- Derive everything domain-specific (names, screens, fields, vocabulary) from the references + requirements + contract — never assume a domain or import another app's vocabulary.
</reference_material>


